# Build artifacts (cl65 drops temp objects in the repo root) + linker map
*.o
*.map
# ...and the two cl65 asks for by name rather than by extension: `-m map.txt` is
# how the segment sizes get read (the $2000-$5FFF window is the scarce thing in
# this cartridge, so that map is consulted often) and `-l` drops a listing beside
# the source. Both are regenerated on demand from tracked sources.
map.txt
src/*.lst

# Build OUTPUTS — every one is regenerated by `make` from tracked sources: the cart
# itself, the asset-compiler blobs, and the stripped VGM command streams. Do NOT add
# madsim.exe or roms/*.bin here: those are built in the SEPARATE MAD-65 repo and
# bundled on purpose so this repo is self-contained. Generated .inc files stay
# tracked (text, diffable).
cart.bin
proto/*/*.bin
assets/*.bin
assets/vgm/*_stream.bin
assets/vgm/*_stream.inc

# ...and the picture `make preview` draws, for the same reason. The one in each
# proto/ IS tracked: a frozen bench's picture is part of its record, while this
# one is redrawn on every check.
/preview.png

# Python tool caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# madsim runtime dumps (F2 register dumps)
dumps/

# Claude Code local config
.claude/
